-- Garry Glendown <sslcrtsrv@mlfwd.de>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000

 sslcrtsrv (0.9.3-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * added netblock allow/deny access lists gating both scs-server and
    scs-acme-server's ports (allowed_networks/denied_networks,
    acme_allowed_networks/acme_denied_networks), with an option for the
    ACME list to check the real client's forwarded address instead of the
    reverse proxy's own
  * added source-IP-based lockout after repeated authentication failures
    on scs-server, scs-acme-server, and the web admin login
  * fixed a TOCTOU race in traditional-protocol nonce consumption
  * added SSLCRTSRV_DB_PASSWORD as an opt-in alternative to a plaintext DB
    password in server_config.json
  * added systemd hardening (NoNewPrivileges, ProtectSystem=strict, etc.)
    to both service units
  * added X-Frame-Options/CSP headers and pinned/scanned dependencies
    (pip-audit in CI)

-- Garry Glendown <sslcrtsrv@mlfwd.de>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0000

sslcrtsrv (0.9.2-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * added trusted-client auto-approval for ACME: an admin can pre-issue an
    EAB or contact-token credential (cltmanager acme_create_eab_grant /
    acme_create_contact_token_grant) that auto-confirms an account and
    auto-approves matching fqdns, skipping acme_confirm/assign entirely
  * fixed scs-acme-server's access log always showing the reverse proxy's
    own address instead of the real client - now honors X-Forwarded-For
    when acme_trusted_proxy_ip is set, same trust boundary as IP-pinning
  * fixed check_schema_is_current() only checking for one past migration's
    column, letting init_database() silently half-upgrade a stale database
    on the next two migrations - now derived from scs-dbmigrate's own
    single up-to-date revision list instead of a second, easily-forgotten
    one
  * unified logging across every tool: console/rotating-log-file/syslog
    now all go through one shared setup (new log_dir/log_max_bytes/
    log_backup_count config fields), replacing crtrequest.py's own
    unrotated, CWD-relative crtrequest.log and giving cltmanager/
    crtmanager/dbmigrate/admintui a persistent audit trail they never had

-- Garry Glendown <sslcrtsrv@mlfwd.de>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0000

sslcrtsrv (0.9.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * added ACME support to admintui: Clients tab shows a Type column and
