-- Garry Glendown <sslcrtsrv@mlfwd.de>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0000


sslcrtsrv (0.9.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * added scs-acme-server: optional RFC 8555 ACME protocol server for
    issuing certificates to third-party ACME clients (requires the new
    `acme` extra / python3-josepy)
  * fixed scs-acme-server (and the classic server) using a TCP accept
    backlog of only 5, causing connections to stall indefinitely behind a
    reverse proxy under load
  * fixed init_database() letting create_all() run against an unmigrated
    database, corrupting its schema into a state scs-dbmigrate couldn't
    cleanly recover from
  * fixed an ACME renewal silently resetting an already-approved fqdns
    permission back to pending, requiring the admin to re-approve every
    single renewal

