sslcrtsrv (0.8.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * fixed scs-dbmigrate migrate building an invalid connection URL for
    mysql/postgresql targets
  * fixed scs-dbmigrate crashing with a raw traceback on a missing
    pymysql/psycopg2 driver or an unreachable target - now a clear error
  * fixed scs-dbmigrate migrate aborting on a pre-existing orphaned
    client_certificate_relations row - now skipped and reported instead
  * fixed a SAWarning during the certificates.id schema upgrade
  * fixed a client's certificate request crashing on MySQL/PostgreSQL with a
    foreign key violation on client_certificate_relations
  * fixed cltmanager assign-permission crashing the same way when granting
    access for a not-yet-issued certificate
  * fixed crtrequest silently recording a fake 2020-01-01 validity date for
    a genuinely-issued certificate whenever the real date couldn't be
    extracted - now fails loudly instead of storing it
  * fixed crtrequest never applying a configured mysql/postgresql backend -
    it silently kept using the default sqlite database on every run, so
    real issuance data never reached a migrated network database
  * Manual updates: fresh MySQL/PostgreSQL setup walkthrough, scs-dbmigrate
    migrate's error handling

