sslcrtsrv (0.1.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging: sslcrtsrv-client and sslcrtsrv-server, built
    from the sslcrtsrv Python distribution (pyproject.toml).
  * Console scripts installed as scs-* (scs-client, scs-server,
    scs-crtmanager, scs-cltmanager, scs-crtrequest, scs-admintui,
    scs-web-admin-bridge) rather than the longer sslcrtsrv-* prefix.
  * setup.cfg's version now reads src/sslcrtsrv/__init__.py's __version__
    directly (attr:) instead of duplicating it, and debian/rules refuses to
    build if this changelog's upstream version doesn't match __version__ -
    catches a bumped __version__ with a forgotten `dch` at build time
    instead of silently shipping a stale-versioned .deb.

 -- Garry Glendown <sslcrtsrv@mlfwd.de>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 17:14:41 +0000
